&lt;p&gt;The photo now fits the screen. Run the snippet from step 3 again: one red box is left, around the booking link.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 7: break the long link
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A browser only breaks a line at a space or at certain punctuation, and the long code at the end of the booking link has neither. &lt;code&gt;overflow-wrap: anywhere&lt;/code&gt; lets it break between any two letters when nothing else fits. Box Kite has no typed prop for it yet, so it goes in &lt;code&gt;css&lt;/code&gt;, the escape hatch for a CSS property without a prop of its own. It still becomes a class, like every other prop:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
